Not kept (fail or hang on main, so not gates; for main issues):
  vm_vec_misalign_directed (review A), vec_idx_misalign_fault_directed (review C): a vector element that is
    both misaligned and on an unmapped page hangs main (TIMEOUT at 4M cycles). vm_vec_misalign: all three
    bus settings on d7fb9a2, d7fb9a2+vro and 9da0006; vec_idx_misalign_fault: no-cache on d7fb9a2 and
    9da0006, random bus on d7fb9a2+vro. Branch off behaves as main; on and ft pass both (the FPGA_TIMING
    VLS path). A main bug.
  walk_preempt_directed (A), vm_walk_race_directed (C, gen_walk_race.py root1): the walker preemption race,
    fail on d7fb9a2 (+vro) and on the branch (off, on, ft), pass on 9da0006 (#74 fix). For after the
    branch merges main.
  instret_page_directed (C): two instret reads three instructions apart across a page boundary must differ
    by 3. Main reads instret in EX and counts retirement at WB, so the delta depends on MEM/WB occupancy;
    FPGA_TIMING's +1 page-change bubble before the second read gives 4 (test 5204, random bus; no-cache
    passes). Main's own read timing, not changed by #53.

